{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Use the existing Spring XD module/component architecture (sources, sinks, processors, jobs) for all new functionality to ensure consistency with the framework.",
    "Implement configuration changes for the hdfs-dataset sink (U2) by extending the existing Avro serialization configuration, adding a codec property that accepts Avro-supported codecs including 'snappy', 'deflate', 'bzip2', and 'null'.",
    "Implement TLS/SSL support for the Mail sink (U3) by adding a 'java-mail-properties' attribute that accepts a Spring <util:properties/> bean reference, following the pattern shown in the Spring Integration Mail reference documentation.",
    "For U4, expose partitionResultsTimeout as a metadata attribute by updating the relevant job metadata XML/schema files for the 3 OOTB jobs (file-jdbc, jdbc-file, jdbc-hdfs) and the parent job metadata definitions.",
    "For U5, perform a coordinated Spring Boot 1.2.0.RELEASE upgrade by updating the parent POM and resolving cascading dependency compatibility issues; treat each of the ~32 listed dependency upgrades as a discrete verification step.",
    "For U6, design a new manifest.yml schema that supports the same properties currently embedded in stream definitions, and implement a resolver that loads manifest properties and merges them into the stream definition context.",
    "For U7, implement message compression as a reusable Spring XD processor module (compress) and decompress module, using java.util.zip for gzip and zip formats; expose the compression type as a module option.",
    "For U8, extend the existing Rabbit source and sink modules by adding a 'compression' option that integrates with the compression/decompression logic from U7.",
    "Assume all work includes unit tests, integration tests, and inline code review; no separate large QA phase beyond the benchmarking task in U1.",
    "Assume Maven is the build system of choice (consistent with the XML dependency listing in U5)."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The developer is fully proficient in Spring XD, Spring Framework 4.x, Spring Boot, Spring Integration, and the JVM ecosystem.",
    "Work-hours represent focused development effort, not calendar time; no waiting, meetings, or blocked time is included beyond a small planning/review allowance.",
    "No major architectural rewrites are required; all changes can be made as additive features or configuration updates within the existing module framework.",
    "U1 (benchmarking) is treated as a development activity because the specification lists it as a deliverable; the effort covers setting up the benchmark, running both Sqoop and jdbchdfs jobs, and producing a comparison document.",
    "U5 dependency upgrade effort assumes a clean upgrade with moderate compatibility friction; it does not include deep redesign of any module that turns out to be incompatible.",
    "Existing test infrastructure (unit, integration, and smoke tests) can be reused for the new functionality with minor additions.",
    "Documentation updates are limited to in-code Javadoc, wiki page edits, and module option reference tables; a full user-guide rewrite is out of scope.",
    "Code review and final integration/regression testing are broken out as separate activities rather than embedded in each user story."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Increment planning and setup",
      "activity_description": "Review specification, set up sprint/increment backlog, prepare development environment, and identify affected modules across the 8 user stories.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Sqoop vs jdbchdfs benchmarking",
      "activity_description": "Configure benchmark workloads, run Sqoop and jdbchdfs batch jobs under comparable conditions, collect throughput/latency/resource metrics, and produce a written comparison report for QA.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Disable snappy / configurable codec for hdfs-dataset Avro sink",
      "activity_description": "Extend the hdfs-dataset sink Avro writer to accept a configurable codec option (snappy, deflate, bzip2, null), add default behavior change to allow disabling snappy, expose module options, and add unit/integration tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 20
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "U3 - TLS/SSL support for Mail sink (IMAP/SMTP)",
      "activity_description": "Add a 'java-mail-properties' attribute to the Mail sink configuration, wire in a Spring <util:properties/> bean for SSL/TLS settings, validate against imaps/smtps test servers, and add unit/integration tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U4 - Expose partitionResultsTimeout as metadata attribute",
      "activity_description": "Update the metadata XML/schema for the affected OOTB jobs (file-jdbc, jdbc-file, jdbc-hdfs and parent) so partitionResultsTimeout is documented and overridable, and update the wiki page accordingly.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U5 - Spring Boot 1.2.0.RELEASE and dependency upgrades",
      "activity_description": "Bump parent Spring Boot version to 1.2.0.RELEASE, update each of the ~32 listed dependency versions in the root POM, resolve API and transitive compatibility issues, run the full module test suite, and fix regressions.",
      "most_likely_effort": 64
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U6 - Separate deployment manifest YML file",
      "activity_description": "Design a manifest.yml schema for deployment manifest properties, implement a loader that resolves the manifest and merges its properties into the stream definition context, preserve backward compatibility, and add tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U7 - Message compression processor module (gzip, zip)",
      "activity_description": "Implement a 'compress' processor and a 'decompress' processor module supporting gzip and zip, expose compression type as a module option, handle streaming payloads, and add unit/integration tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "U8 - Rabbit source and sink compression",
      "activity_description": "Add a 'compression' option to the Rabbit source (decompress on receipt) and Rabbit sink (compress on send) modules, integrate with the U7 compression codec, and add unit/integration tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "Cross-feature integration testing",
      "activity_description": "Run end-to-end stream tests combining the upgraded Boot stack, manifest loading, compression processors, and the Rabbit compression option together to verify no regressions in composite flows.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "Code review and refactoring",
      "activity_description": "Self/peer review of all changesets across the 8 user stories and light refactoring to keep code style consistent with the rest of the codebase.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "Documentation updates",
      "activity_description": "Update module reference docs, wiki pages, sample stream definitions, and the manifest format documentation to reflect the new features (codec option, java-mail-properties, partitionResultsTimeout, manifest, compression, Rabbit compression).",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 260
  }
}
```

